.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_MSDOSFS 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_msdosfs
.Nd mount a FAT file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ls
.Op Fl D Ar DOS_codepage
.Op Fl g Ar gid
.Op Fl L Ar locale
.Op Fl M Ar mask
.Op Fl m Ar mask
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Op Fl u Ar uid
.Ar special node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
mounts the FAT12, FAT16 or FAT32 file system on device
.Ar special
at directory
.Ar node
.Pq Xr msdosfs 5 .
It is
.Xr mount 8
.Fl t Cm msdosfs ,
and its flags may also be given as
.Xr fstab 5
options, as on
.Fx :
.Ql -m=644,-M=755 .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl u Ar uid
The owner of every file, a user name or number; by default the owner of
.Ar node .
.It Fl g Ar gid
The group of every file, a group name or number; by default the group of
.Ar node .
.It Fl m Ar mask
The permissions of every file, in octal; by default those of
.Ar node .
A file with FAT's read-only attribute has its write bits cleared.
.It Fl M Ar mask
The permissions of every directory; by default
.Fl m Ns 's .
.It Fl s
Show and make short (8.3) names only, ignoring long names.
.It Fl l
Show and make long names (the default).
.It Fl L Ar locale
The locale whose character set names are given in.
OxideBSD's
.Nm msdosfs
speaks only UTF-8: a locale with another code set is refused.
.It Fl D Ar DOS_codepage
The code page short names are in, CP437 by default: one of the files in
.Pa /usr/share/msdosfs ,
such as
.Cm CP850 ,
.Cm CP866
or
.Cm CP932 .
.It Fl o Ar options
Options as
.Xr mount 8
takes them; the kernel's names for the flags above are
.Cm uid ,
.Cm gid ,
.Cm mask ,
.Cm dirmask ,
.Cm shortnames ,
.Cm longnames
and
.Cm cs_dos .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/share/msdosfs -compact
.It Pa /usr/share/msdosfs
Code page tables, from the Unicode Consortium's Microsoft mappings.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount a USB stick for user
.Ql user :
.Dl mount_msdosfs -u user -m 644 -M 755 /dev/da0s1 /mnt
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr msdosfs 5 ,
.Xr fsck_msdosfs 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.Nx 0.9 .
.Sh BUGS
.Fx Ns 's
.Fl 9
and
.Fl W
are not supported.
